.TH KINTSUGI-LEDGER 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-ledger \- accepted work ledger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi ledger
list [\-\-kind <type>] [\-\-json]
.br
.B kintsugi ledger
add
.br
.B kintsugi ledger
export [\-\-file <path>]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the accepted work ledger. The ledger tracks plans, artifacts, and
decisions the operator has accepted.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP \fBlist\fR
Show accepted work, newest first
.IP \fBadd\fR
Append one accepted entry
.IP \fBexport\fR
Write the ledger as JSONL
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-kind\fR
Filter by entry type
.IP \fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON
.IP \fB\-\-file\fR
Output file path (export)
.SH EXAMPLES
List entries:
.PP
  $ kintsugi ledger list
.PP
Filter by kind:
.PP
  $ kintsugi ledger list --kind plan
.PP
Add an entry:
.PP
  $ kintsugi ledger add
.PP
Export as JSONL:
.PP
  $ kintsugi ledger export --out ledger.jsonl
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-recall (1)
